{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Take all the chiefs of the people.</b> To judge those who served Peor." "<b>And impale them.</b> Those who served Peor." "<b>And impale.</b> It is hanging, as we find concerning the sons of Saul: ״וְהוֹקַעֲנוּם לַה״ (II Samuel 21:6), and there hanging is explicit (Sanhedrin 34a); one who worships idolatry is stoned, and all who are stoned are hanged (Sanhedrin 45b)." "<b>Before the sun.</b> In the sight of all. And another interpretation: the sun informs the sinners — the cloud folded away from opposite him and the sun shone upon him."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:40.984267821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}